WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:00.983
Instructor: All right.

00:00.983 --> 00:02.940
So let's try using the git stash command,

00:02.940 --> 00:06.900
or git stash save, in order to add our unstaged

00:06.900 --> 00:09.990
and staged changes to the stash.

00:09.990 --> 00:14.070
So back here, I've got our Goodbye World

00:14.070 --> 00:15.390
that I've changed, right?

00:15.390 --> 00:18.210
Goodbye World and Goodbye up in the title.

00:18.210 --> 00:21.180
And this is on the branch called Goodbye.

00:21.180 --> 00:22.740
That's where I am right now.

00:22.740 --> 00:24.990
But I have not committed those changes.

00:24.990 --> 00:28.837
Let's also do one more thing, like maybe in my app.css,

00:28.837 --> 00:31.770
I'm gonna make the body have a background color

00:31.770 --> 00:34.956
that's really obvious, background color of,

00:34.956 --> 00:37.530
I don't know, magenta.

00:37.530 --> 00:39.750
And again, this doesn't really matter if you don't know CSS,

00:39.750 --> 00:42.743
but I've made a very obvious background color magenta,

00:42.743 --> 00:45.570
and it says "Goodbye World!!" up here

00:45.570 --> 00:47.130
and the title is Goodbye.

00:47.130 --> 00:48.960
So those are the changes I've made.

00:48.960 --> 00:51.104
And I need to switch to master right now

00:51.104 --> 00:52.710
for whatever reason,

00:52.710 --> 00:54.930
and I don't wanna take these changes with me,

00:54.930 --> 00:57.330
not to mention the fact that they actually conflict.

00:57.330 --> 01:00.764
I can't take at least the index HTML change with me,

01:00.764 --> 01:02.407
because as we saw previously,

01:02.407 --> 01:05.704
it conflicts with what we have on the master branch.

01:05.704 --> 01:09.390
So I don't want to commit. I'm going to use git stash.

01:09.390 --> 01:10.590
So if I type git status,

01:10.590 --> 01:13.170
if I can actually type it correctly,

01:13.170 --> 01:15.810
you can see two files that have been modified.

01:15.810 --> 01:19.620
I'm going to call git stash save, or just git stash.

01:19.620 --> 01:20.453
Same thing.

01:21.570 --> 01:24.300
And it tells me "Saved working directory and index state."

01:24.300 --> 01:28.138
Index is just what Git calls the staging area.

01:28.138 --> 01:32.670
So it saved the staged and unstaged changes on this branch,

01:32.670 --> 01:34.320
but it did not commit them.

01:34.320 --> 01:37.950
So if I type git status now, we don't see anything,

01:37.950 --> 01:40.170
nothing to commit, working tree clean.

01:40.170 --> 01:42.097
And if I take a look at my files here,

01:42.097 --> 01:43.980
we're back to Hello World!

01:43.980 --> 01:45.750
We don't have the magenta at all,

01:45.750 --> 01:48.630
and if I refresh the page, it's gone.

01:48.630 --> 01:50.820
So those changes are not here.

01:50.820 --> 01:53.259
And now, I could switch to whatever branch I need to,

01:53.259 --> 01:56.460
git switch master, which remember, earlier,

01:56.460 --> 01:58.740
it said I couldn't do because of conflicts.

01:58.740 --> 02:00.614
Now, I'm on the master branch,

02:00.614 --> 02:04.050
we can see here's our Hello World! from before

02:04.050 --> 02:05.700
with all the exclamation points.

02:05.700 --> 02:08.670
And then I could go anywhere else,

02:08.670 --> 02:10.740
I could apply these changes here if I wanted,

02:10.740 --> 02:13.560
or I can go back to the branch I was on before.

02:13.560 --> 02:16.623
So git switch back to goodbye,

02:17.760 --> 02:19.920
and this is what we're dealing with on goodbye.

02:19.920 --> 02:22.170
And if I want to then get those changes back

02:22.170 --> 02:26.520
that I've stashed away, we use git stash pop.

02:26.520 --> 02:29.040
So this will take the most recently stashed changes,

02:29.040 --> 02:31.170
and yes, we can have multiple things in the stash,

02:31.170 --> 02:33.284
we'll get to that, but most frequently,

02:33.284 --> 02:35.910
most commonly, in my experience, we just have one,

02:35.910 --> 02:37.980
I have one thing in the stash at a time.

02:37.980 --> 02:39.960
Anyway, so I'm gonna reapply those changes

02:39.960 --> 02:42.102
to my working copy, which is right here.

02:42.102 --> 02:44.850
git status, just to show you.

02:44.850 --> 02:46.410
It says "nothing to commit."

02:46.410 --> 02:48.330
We don't see that magenta in here.

02:48.330 --> 02:50.280
We don't see Goodbye World.

02:50.280 --> 02:55.280
And now, git stash pop and it tells me,

02:55.470 --> 02:58.590
okay, we added those changes back in for you.

02:58.590 --> 03:00.570
You modified this file, app.css.

03:00.570 --> 03:02.370
You modified index HTML.

03:02.370 --> 03:06.120
And now, if I take a look at my file, it says goodbye again.

03:06.120 --> 03:08.610
If I look at app.css, it has magenta in there.

03:08.610 --> 03:11.430
If I refresh my page, we see those changes now

03:11.430 --> 03:13.740
in the browser where I'm viewing the webpage.

03:13.740 --> 03:15.242
Cool.

03:15.242 --> 03:16.890
So we successfully stashed some changes

03:16.890 --> 03:18.450
and then we applied them.

03:18.450 --> 03:19.593
We popped them off.

03:20.581 --> 03:22.020
All right, so next up, I'll show you some more examples,

03:22.020 --> 03:25.743
and we'll talk about some other stash-related commands.
